  "title": "Schweizer SGS 2-33A — Normal Procedures and Launch Emergencies",
  "description": "A glider, included to exercise the parts of the schema that a powered-aeroplane corpus never reaches: no engine, a launch phase with no equivalent in powered flight, and emergency procedures that are entirely about the tow. Wording is the contributor's own; procedures reflect ordinary US club practice for the type.",
